  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 127 PM EDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nA weak shortwave and brief shot of elevated WAA may bring a few \nsprinkles or light high based showers to nw IN and srn MI this \nafternoon into this evening. Upper level ridging then briefly builds \ninto the lower Great Lakes later tonight into Saturday in between \nsystems. High level clouds will overspread the area on Saturday as \nthe remnants of Hurricane Isaias lift north into the western TN \nValley. Southerly winds will make for a warmer day otherwise on \nSaturday with highs mid 70s to near 80F. \n\nThe remnants of the tropical system then take a more northeasterly \njog through the lower Ohio River Valley Saturday night into Sunday. \nSpoke of energy and associated deeper moisture on its northern \nfringe should bring at least light rain in the vicinity of an \ninverted trough, mainly late Saturday evening into Sunday morning. \nThe NBM and GEFS/ECMWF ensembles have 50-80% probs for rainfall \ntotals up to near a half inch in northwest OH, especially in the \nLima area. QPF and PoPs do drop off along and west of the Interstate \n69 corridor with a sharp cut-off to the rain possible in nw IN and \nsw MI. No hazardous wx anticipated regardless with lingering clouds \nlikely keeping Sunday's highs cooler (mid 60s to low 70s). \n\nAnother round of height rises and warmer low level southwest flow \nwill make Monday the warmest day of the 7 day forecast with highs in \nthe upper 70s to mid 80s. A weak cool front likely drops \nthrough later Monday night into Tuesday morning with slightly \ncooler temps and a low chance (20-40%) for a few showers. The \npattern does look to become increasingly active for the second \nhalf of the week with gusty winds and periodic rain/thunder \nchances. The phasing of incoming northern and southern stream \nsystems to carve out a deep trough and potential strong sfc \nreflection over the northern Great Lakes and Ontario. This \nlikely drives a strong fall cold front through with \ncool/blustery air filtering in sometime Friday into Saturday.",
